					<p></p><ul>
<li>Rugged Inductotherm=C2=AE steel shell induction furnaces</li>
<li>Rapid-exchange features for maximum productivity</li>
<li>Efficient Inductotherm power supplies and auxiliary stirring</li>
<li>Multiple chamber systems: mold chambers, charging chambers, and hot tun=
dish insertion chambers optimize productivity through the melt chamber</li>
<li>Multiple charging systems (horizontal side charger and top charger) for=
 rapid feeding of a variety of charge materials are available to optimize m=
elting speed and maximize efficiency</li>
<li>Multiple mold pouring via mold cars or turntables</li>
<li>High-conductance wetted filters to protect vacuum pumps and minimize fi=
re hazards</li>
<li>Intuitive PC-based HMI and PLC-based controls with full SCADA</li>
<li>Remote furnace operation via CCTV from the control room for improved sa=
fety</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Vacuum System:</strong></p>
<p>Three-stage vacuum pumping systems incorporating oil-sealed rotary pumps=
 or dry-type screw pumps, roots-type mechanical blowers, and oil vapor boos=
ter pumps for finalizing vacuum levels in the 10<sup>-3</sup> torr (0.0013 =
mbar | 0.13 Pa) range.</p>
<p><strong>Mold Pouring:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Hot tundish insertion chargers configured to insert an externally prehe=
ated refractory tundish into the pour position within a few minutes</li>
<li>Programmable control of mold car / turntable movement with auto-indexin=
g</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Straight Pouring Design:</strong></p>
<p>Consarc designs all VIM furnaces so that the tundish is in line with the=
 direction of the pour and does not require use of a launder as is required=
 in tilting chamber-type systems, which provides many metallurgical and fin=
ancial benefits.</p>
<p><strong>Controls:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Computerized control and SCADA systems</li>
<li>TV cameras on remotely actuated sight ports for remote operation</li>
</ul>
